    {
      "id": "9fec5c18-e8a9-4546-9c77-c6bf92192957",
      "name": "Overview",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        4672,
        1808
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 1100,
        "height": 608,
        "content": "## Answer currency rate questions from Gmail and chat with a cached AI agent\n\n**Who's it for**\nAnyone who wants a reusable pattern for an AI agent that serves several channels and avoids paying for the same model call twice. Exchange rates are only the example: swap the tool for any read-only API.\n\n**How it works**\n1. Chat and Gmail messages are normalized to the same fields and processed one at a time.\n2. The workflow detects two ISO currency codes (for example \"USD to EUR\") and looks for a fresh cached answer for that pair and date.\n3. On a cache hit the model is not called. On a miss, a Gemini agent queries the free Frankfurter API and the answer is cached.\n4. Every query is logged (channel, cache hit, latency) so you can measure the savings. The reply goes back through the channel it came from.\n\n**How to set up**\n- Create the Data Table **Currency cache** with columns `cache_key` (string), `pair` (string), `response` (string), `cached_at` (number).\n- Create the Data Table **Query log** with columns `logged_at` (string), `source` (string), `pair` (string), `cache_hit` (boolean), `latency_ms` (number).\n- Select the tables in the 3 Data Table nodes and add your Gemini and Gmail credentials.\n- Review the **Set configurable variables** node and the filter in **Receive email from Gmail**.\n\n**Requirements**\nGoogle Gemini API key, Gmail account, n8n with Data Tables. Frankfurter needs no API key.\n\n**How to customize**\nReplace the **Get Exchange Rate** tool and the agent prompt, and adapt **Build cache key** so that equivalent questions produce the same key."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "dfac044f-fb98-4fdd-a71a-af247dc16cee",
      "name": "Step 1 - Receive and normalize",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        4672,
        2448
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 768,
        "height": 176,
        "content": "## 1. Receive and normalize\nChat and Gmail messages are converted to the same fields (`sessionId`, `chatInput`, `source`, `email`). The loop handles one message at a time, so several emails in one poll are safe."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "fdd924ed-c782-4f78-8ae7-f3cf14880cd1",
      "name": "Step 2 - Check cache",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        5472,
        2448
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 1296,
        "height": 176,
        "content": "## 2. Look for a fresh cached answer\nThe key is built from the two currency codes found in the message, in order (first = base, second = target), plus today's date. Messages without exactly two codes skip the cache. The time-to-live is set in **Set configurable variables**."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "570cf5f5-3acf-4815-925c-788d7593d74f",
      "name": "Step 3 - Ask agent and save",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        6800,
        2448
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 1472,
        "height": 176,
        "content": "## 3. Ask the AI agent only on a cache miss\nThe agent calls the Frankfurter API. Answers are cached only if they contain a number, so questions and error messages are never stored. If the agent fails, a fallback message is sent instead."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "c445b801-6600-4835-abb2-03e6ff2dcc49",
      "name": "Step 4 - Log and reply",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        8320,
        2448
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 768,
        "height": 176,
        "content": "## 4. Log and reply\nEvery query is logged. The reply returns through the channel it came from (chat or email)."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "c4b3a3ec-8c8f-4027-8ba7-250440ddd082",
      "name": "Good to know",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        5808,
        1808
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 1024,
        "height": 288,
        "content": "## Good to know\n- Rates are **daily reference rates** (about 16:00 CET), not live quotes. Check supported currencies at `https://api.frankfurter.dev/v1/currencies`.\n- Write two ISO codes in the order **base, then target** (\"USD to EUR\"). Names like \"dollar\" skip the cache because they can be ambiguous.\n- The cache is **shared by all users**: use it only with read-only, non-personal data.\n- Anyone who matches the Gmail filter gets a reply: restrict senders if you publish this.\n- Cached answers keep the language of the first request."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
